The only query that fully satisfies the “clean up its URL (removing extra slashes) and extracting the correct page path” requirement is 0result.sql – it strips query‑strings / fragments before counting, collapses duplicated slashes, and then ranks the results.  
Both 1result.sql and 2result.sql keep any ?query or #fragment in the path, so identical pages with different parameters would be counted separately, which violates the task definition.

```plaintext
0result.sql
